# Your live Worker config, holding your Cloudflare account id, KV namespace
# ids, and custom domain. Copied from wrangler.jsonc.example on `npm install`;
# fill in your own values. The tracked template is wrangler.jsonc.example.
wrangler.jsonc

# Generated at build time from the wrangler config's routes[0].pattern — never
# committed, so it cannot go stale. See scripts/write-hostname.mjs.
src/deployed-hostname.generated.ts

# GSD planning/state artifacts — internal process notes, not part of the
# public project. Excluded from the open-source repo; kept locally for the
# GSD workflow. Also carries personal data (calendar names/ids) that the
# forbidden-tokens scan does not cover.
.planning/
.gsd/

# Live-account observation logs, deliberately not tracked.
#
# An earlier copy of this path was deleted on 2026-08-16 and five findings were
# salvaged into .planning/phases/02-imap-client-mail-read/02-UAT.md:823, on the
# reasoning that "a second, diverging account of server behaviour is worse than
# none" — roughly half of it described this client's own pre-fix behaviour as
# though it described the iCloud server. The file reappeared untracked and was
# re-examined under plan 03-10; its DAV-era section 10 was found to be already
# recorded, more completely, in 03-01-SUMMARY.md, so there was nothing left to
# salvage. Ignored rather than merely deleted so it cannot drift back in as an
# untracked file and re-raise the same settled question.
#
# The authoritative account of observed server behaviour is the phase UAT
# document (02-UAT.md for mail, 03-UAT.md for DAV) — not a file under
# test/fixtures/, which is read by no test despite its location.
test/fixtures/OBSERVED-BEHAVIOUR.md
